ta-id=\"b8c696a\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #0000ff; text-decoration: underline;\"><em>Phase 3 Note: <\/em><\/span><\/strong><\/span><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong><span style=\"color: #0000ff; text-decoration: underline;\"><em>Certain policies within the Innovation Office Manual have since been updated for alignment with the Utah Supreme Court&#8217;s Phase 2 guidance. Updates include a revised consumer disclosure policy, revised fee policy ($5,000 annual fee), streamlined data metrics, retirement of the licensing policy, criminal history guidelines, and the new Utah Innovation Requirement.\u00a0 Please also note that the Supreme Court closed the alternative business structure (ABS)-only portion of the Sandbox.\u00a0<\/em> <em>The LSI Committee will be considering additional policy changes in line with the Court\u2019s guidance.<\/em><\/span><\/strong><\/span><\/p><p>The Innovation Office Manual is a working document.\u00a0 As a pilot program, the policies and requirements of the Sandbox are iterative; changes are made as more information is gathered.\u00a0\u00a0<\/p><p>The Innovation Office Manual contains the policies and procedures of the Office of Legal Services Innovation of the Utah State Bar through which it executes the Utah Supreme Court&#8217;s mandate to assist with regulating non-traditional legal services and entities along with the Court\u2019s Legal Services Innovation Committee.<\/p><p style=\"color: #635f5f;\"><span style=\"color: var( --e-global-color-text ); font-family: var( --e-global-typography-text-font-family ), Sans-serif; font-weight: var( --e-global-typography-text-font-weight );\">The Innovation Office Manual was updated on February 20, 2024 to reflect the following:<\/span><\/p><ul style=\"color: #635f5f;\"><li>Updated definitions for Controlling and Financing Persons (see page 6)<\/li><li>Discretionary requirement for credit checks (see page 9)<\/li><\/ul>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-41b59a8 elementor-widget elementor-widget-spacer\" data-id=\"41b59a8\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"spacer.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-spacer\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-spacer-inner\"><\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-0abc3b6 elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default\" data-id=\"0abc3b6\" data-element_type=\"section\" data-e-type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-18185b8\" data-id=\"18185b8\" data-element_type=\"column\" data-e-type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-bc3b655 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"bc3b655\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">Rule 14-810. Non-traditional Legal Providers Assisting Clients in Court<br><\/h2>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-inner-section elementor-element elementor-element-576b9be elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-hei